-- 0840 · The faith demo: Aarav Patni is enrolled too (owner, 2026-10-15): the Patni family has all three children in the Learning Center.
--
-- Pack demo_faith_jain_v1 goes to version 5. Aarav (5), who was on the waitlist, joins Dev (9) and Maya (8) in the class Anita Bhandari teaches
-- ("Introduction to Jainism", Room B), so he is in her roster and attendance list and, with his brother and sister, in the family's member app.
-- Same pattern as 0820: the pack is data, generated by supabase/scripts/build-demo-packs.mjs; the community that exists is brought in line in place
-- (no center is deleted or recreated; same id, same QuickBooks connection and account mapping, same demo sign-ins).
--
-- THE AGE CONFLICT, SAID PLAINLY. The class's level is for ages 8 to 10 and Aarav is 5 (the demo's Level 1, "Level 1 · Room A", is for ages 5 to 7). The
-- platform never places a child outside a level's band by itself: its registration sends such a child to the office (app._pathshala_plan and
-- app._pathshala_seat_or_wait: the outcome is "office"), and the office, a person, may place them by hand. The pack shows exactly that and no more: Aarav's enrollment has
-- the channel "office", the level his family asked for (Level 1), his class, and a note that says it. The age band is not changed and nothing is bent: the
-- database does not refuse a hand placement, the registration just never makes one. Capacity is fine (6 of 15 places).
--
-- THE FEE, BY THE PLATFORM'S OWN RULE (app._pathshala_price): children are ranked by their level fee, then oldest first; every child after the first has
-- the term's sibling discount (10%); the family cap ($400.00) limits the total. The term fee is $150.00, so: Dev $150.00; Maya $150.00 less $15.00 =
-- $135.00; Aarav $150.00 less $15.00 = $135.00, less $20.00 more because $150.00 + $135.00 + $135.00 = $420.00 is over the cap, so $115.00. The family
-- owes $400.00 in all, in whole cents (15000 + 13500 + 11500), as three open fee pledges due in 14 days. With Aarav no longer waiting, the principal's
-- waitlist item is gone (her other item, Zara's registration to place, stays).
--
-- THE LIVE DEMO. The new rows are loaded by the pack at the community's next reset: Platform > Setup > Demo sign-in > Start over loads them now, or the
-- nightly check does (3 a.m. in its time zone, or at once if it was last loaded over 30 hours ago) when a change not made by a job is on record for the
-- community. This migration writes one such audit entry for every faith demo community still on an older pack ("demo.pack_updated"), so the nightly
-- check reloads it without anyone pressing anything. It also runs app.demo_align_center (0820), which changes nothing when the community is already in
-- line. No policy, grant, permission or money rule of any object is changed.

